{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Elim</b> <b>and they came, etc., to the Wilderness of Sin.</b> Scripture took a short route, for when they journeyed from Elim they encamped by the Sea of Reeds — \"and they journeyed from the Sea of Reeds and encamped in the Wilderness of Sin\" (Numbers 33:10–11) — for this wilderness is large, extending from Elim to Sinai. When they journeyed from Elim they encamped by the Sea of Reeds in that wilderness, and they journeyed from the shore of the sea and entered into the midst of the wilderness and made stages in it: Dophkah and Alush (Numbers 33:12–13), and they journeyed from Alush, which is in the Wilderness of Sinai, and encamped at Rephidim (Numbers 33:14). According to the opinion of our Sages (Exodus Rabbah 25:5), the matter of the manna took place at Alush, for when they saw that they were encamping and journeying and encamping in the wilderness at Dophkah and Alush and had not departed from it, they became afraid and complained. This is the meaning of \"and they complained in the wilderness,\" for there was no complaint on the day they arrived there, but only while they were in the wilderness." "The meaning of <b>which is between Elim and Sinai</b> is to distinguish this Wilderness of Sin from the other Wilderness of Zin (Numbers 20:1), which Scripture spells with a צ, where they arrived in the fortieth year and Miriam died there. Therefore there it says \"and they encamped in the Wilderness of Zin, that is Kadesh\" (Numbers 33:36), to distinguish it from this one."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:55.929590498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}